From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v10 001] panvk: expose 32 vertex input attributes
Generated-by: LLM

Purpose: maxVertexInputAttributes/maxVertexInputBindings were pinned to the
 Vulkan minimum of 16 (MAX_VBS), which is our own bookkeeping limit: the Mali
 hardware supports up to 2^9 vertex attributes (see the comment above
 .maxVertexInputAttributes in panvk_vX_physical_device.c).  D3D11 - and
 therefore DXVK - needs 32 input elements, so games that use more than 16
 attributes could not create a pipeline.
 .
 Raise MAX_VBS (bindings + attribute table) and MAX_VS_ATTRIBS (MALI_ATTRIBUTE
 slots reserved in the VS driver set, images follow them on pre-Valhall) to 32,
 and allow vertex shader input locations up to MAX_VS_ATTRIBS.  The Bifrost
 attribute_count computation is switched to the 64-bit mask so sparse
 locations above 15 are still counted correctly there.
 .
 Nothing is spoofed: the attribute descriptors are actually emitted for all
 32 locations on CSF (prepare_vs_driver_set loops over MAX_VS_ATTRIBS and
 vk_vertex_input_state supports 32 attributes), the limit reported to
 applications matches what the driver implements.
Source/Reference: Mesa 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b,
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h (MAX_VBS),
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_shader.h (MAX_VS_ATTRIBS),
 src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c (prepare_vs_driver_set)
Tested GPU: none yet (compile-level)
Tested Kbase UAPI: n/a
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b
Dependencies: none
Validation test: panvk-test vertex attribute stress with 32 locations

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h
index ff34da3..5b25d5a 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h
@@ -27,7 +27,11 @@
 #include "pan_fb.h"
 #include "pan_props.h"
 
-#define MAX_VBS 16
+/* The hardware supports up to 2^9 vertex attributes/bindings, only our own
+ * bookkeeping limits this.  Expose 32 attributes, which is what D3D11
+ * (and therefore DXVK) needs, instead of the Vulkan minimum of 16.
+ */
+#define MAX_VBS 32
 
 #if PAN_ARCH < 10
 #define MAX_FRAMEBUFFER_DIMENSION (1 << 14)
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_shader.h b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_shader.h
index fabb9a9..f8aa45e 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_shader.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_shader.h
@@ -27,7 +27,12 @@
 extern const struct vk_device_shader_ops panvk_per_arch(device_shader_ops);
 
 #define MAX_RTS 8
-#define MAX_VS_ATTRIBS 16
+/* Number of MALI_ATTRIBUTE slots reserved at the start of the VS attribute
+ * table (images are placed right after this range on pre-Valhall).  The
+ * hardware supports up to 2^9 attributes, so 32 is a safe software limit and
+ * matches the D3D11 limit.
+ */
+#define MAX_VS_ATTRIBS 32
 
 #if PAN_ARCH < 9
 
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
index ae29960..1e2b7ec 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
@@ -1112,11 +1112,11 @@ panvk_compile_nir(struct panvk_device *dev, nir_shader *nir,
        * opposite. Patch attribute_count accordingly, so
        * pan_shader_prepare_rsd() does what we expect.
        */
-      uint32_t gen_attribs =
-         (shader->info.attributes_read & VERT_BIT_GENERIC_ALL) >>
-         VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC0;
+      uint64_t gen_attribs =
+         (shader->info.attributes_read >> VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC0) &
+         BITFIELD64_MASK(MAX_VS_ATTRIBS);
 
-      shader->info.attribute_count = util_last_bit(gen_attribs);
+      shader->info.attribute_count = util_last_bit64(gen_attribs);
 
       /* NULL IDVS shaders are not allowed. */
       if (!bin_size)
@@ -1471,7 +1471,7 @@ panvk_compile_shader(struct panvk_device *dev,
           */
          nir_foreach_shader_in_variable(var, nir) {
             assert(var->data.location >= VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC0 &&
-                   var->data.location <= VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC15);
+                   var->data.location < VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC0 + MAX_VS_ATTRIBS);
             var->data.driver_location =
                var->data.location - VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC0;
          }
